ecause service config is disabled\r\n2022/03/25 18:09:40 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] ClientConn switching balancer to \"pick_first\".     // <--- it goes to wrong here, should be \"grpclb\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:09:40 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel switches to new LB policy \"pick_first\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:09:40 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel Connectivity change to TRANSIENT_FAILURE\r\n2022/03/25 18:09:40 INFO: [core] pickfirstBalancer: ResolverError called with error produced zero addresses\r\n2022/03/25 18:09:40 could not greet: rpc error: code = Unavailable desc = name resolver error: produced zero addresses\r\n```\r\nWe find that in the v1.26.0, it works fine. so, the newer version has this bug. here is logs after fix the bug:\r\n```\r\n$$$$ ./greeter_client -addr dns:///anti.52tt.local\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel created\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] original dial target is: \"dns:///anti.52tt.local\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] parsed dial target is: {Scheme:dns Authority: Endpoint:anti.52tt.local URL:{Scheme:dns Opaque: User: Host: Path:/anti.52tt.local RawPath: ForceQuery:false RawQuery: Fragment: RawFragment:}}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel authority set to \"anti.52tt.local\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Resolver state updated: {\r\n  \"Addresses\": null,\r\n  \"ServiceConfig\": null,\r\n  \"Attributes\": {}\r\n} ()\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] ignoring service config from resolver (<nil>) and applying the default because service config is disabled\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] ClientConn switching balancer to \"grpclb\". // <---- fix, it works\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel switches to new LB policy \"grpclb\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [grpclb] lbBalancer: UpdateClientConnState: {ResolverState:{Addresses:[] ServiceConfig:<nil> Attributes:0xc00000e328} BalancerConfig:<nil>}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Channel created\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] original dial target is: \"grpclb-internal:///grpclb.subClientConn\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] parsed dial target is: {Scheme:grpclb-internal Authority: Endpoint:grpclb.subClientConn URL:{Scheme:grpclb-internal Opaque: User: Host: Path:/grpclb.subClientConn RawPath: ForceQuery:false RawQuery: Fragment: RawFragment:}}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Channel authority set to \"grpclb.subClientConn\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Resolver state updated: {\r\n  \"Addresses\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"Addr\": \"10.102.214.133:9999\",\r\n      \"ServerName\": \"grpclb-pro-new.52tt.local.\",\r\n      \"Attributes\": null,\r\n      \"BalancerAttributes\": null,\r\n      \"Type\": 0,\r\n      \"Metadata\": null\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"ServiceConfig\": null,\r\n  \"Attributes\": null\r\n} (resolver returned new addresses)\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] ClientConn switching balancer to \"pick_first\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Channel switches to new LB policy \"pick_first\"\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2 SubChannel #3] Subchannel created\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] blockingPicker: the picked transport is not ready, loop back to repick\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2 SubChannel #3] Subchannel Connectivity change to CONNECTING\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2 SubChannel #3] Subchannel picks a new address \"10.102.214.133:9999\" to connect\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] pickfirstBalancer: UpdateSubConnState: 0xc000260a60, {CONNECTING <nil>}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Channel Connectivity change to CONNECTING\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2 SubChannel #3] Subchannel Connectivity change to READY\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] pickfirstBalancer: UpdateSubConnState: 0xc000260a60, {READY <nil>}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 Channel #2] Channel Connectivity change to READY\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [grpclb] lbBalancer: processing server list: servers:{ip_address:\"\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\xff\\xff\\n\\n\\t\\x86\"  port:80  load_balance_token:\"10.10.9.134:80_1648232525\"}\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [grpclb] lbBalancer: server list entry[0]: ipStr:|10.10.9.134|, port:|80|, load balancer token:|10.10.9.134:80_1648232525|\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 SubChannel #5] Subchannel created\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel Connectivity change to CONNECTING\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 SubChannel #5] Subchannel Connectivity change to CONNECTING\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 SubChannel #5] Subchannel picks a new address \"10.10.9.134:80\" to connect\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [grpclb] lbBalancer: handle SubConn state change: 0xc00038e060, CONNECTING\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1 SubChannel #5] Subchannel Connectivity change to READY\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [grpclb] lbBalancer: handle SubConn state change: 0xc00038e060, READY\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 INFO: [core] [Channel #1] Channel Connectivity change to READY\r\n2022/03/25 18:22:05 could not greet: rpc error: code = NotFound desc = method /helloworld.Greeter/SayHello is not supported\r\n```\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/5276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/5276/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/5048","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/